WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.305
Tully's been here.

3
00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:22.267
We found one of their camps just ahead.

4
00:02:23.518 --> 00:02:26.521
But something strange has happened there.

5
00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.228
They're all Rivermen.

6
00:03:08.313 --> 00:03:09.356
Who killed them?

7
00:03:10.607 --> 00:03:12.317
We found no sign of their foe.

8
00:03:29.918 --> 00:03:31.503
They did not fall here.

9
00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:39.636
On your guard!

10
00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.430
It's a trap!

11
00:03:56.027 --> 00:03:57.195
To me!

12
00:05:10.727 --> 00:05:12.229
We light the way!

13
00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:15.273
We light the way!

14
00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:35.585
This was not the battle.

15
00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:44.845
Who are they?

16
00:05:45.971 --> 00:05:47.430
Our death.

17
00:05:50.976 --> 00:05:52.477
Criston Cole!

18
00:05:54.688 --> 00:05:59.025
Traitor. usurper. and defiler of justice.

19
00:05:59.109 --> 00:06:00.902
Come forth to hear your fate.

20
00:06:01.528 --> 00:06:04.573
If I strike my banners.
will you spare my men their lives?

21
00:06:05.407 --> 00:06:07.993
I made a promise to the dead. Cole.

22
00:06:08.076 --> 00:06:10.662
I told them I'd build a sept
out of traitors' bones.

23
00:06:11.538 --> 00:06:13.206
I don't have near enough bones yet.

24
00:06:21.882 --> 00:06:24.676
If there is to be battle here.
many of you will die as well.

25
00:06:25.302 --> 00:06:26.720
That's why we've come.

26
00:06:26.803 --> 00:06:30.640
What better way to die than blade in hand?

27
00:06:34.936 --> 00:06:36.354
As you will it.

28
00:06:55.707 --> 00:06:57.542
Let us begin here then.

29
00:06:59.502 --> 00:07:01.296
One of me against the two of you.

30
00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:06.426
Will that be enough to make a fight of it?

31
00:08:07.278 --> 00:08:08.571
They're here.

32
00:08:19.457 --> 00:08:22.460
I mourn my friend Ser Luthor.

33
00:08:22.544 --> 00:08:25.130
and some four and 10 of his best men.

34
00:08:25.213 --> 00:08:26.798
A total count of five and 20
of the City Watch

35
00:08:26.881 --> 00:08:28.717
now slain in the name of "King Daeron."

36
00:08:29.718 --> 00:08:33.138
Lord Ormund mocks us in our own city.

37
00:08:33.221 --> 00:08:37.517
He means to show the realm
that I cannot govern even my own seat.

38
00:08:38.143 --> 00:08:41.270
The great houses watch
while he humiliates me.

39
00:08:41.354 --> 00:08:42.522
Where is my army?

40
00:08:43.273 --> 00:08:44.983
Ser Criston has hindered them.

41
00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:48.945
The vanguard is still a fortnight's march
from Tumbleton.

42
00:08:49.029 --> 00:08:50.321
The insult must be answered now.

43
00:08:50.405 --> 00:08:51.698
We must do what we should
have done in the first.

44
00:08:51.781 --> 00:08:53.366
Burn the villains out.

45
00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:55.118
Then Ormund gets what he wants.

46
00:08:55.744 --> 00:08:58.621
A queen who murders loyal subjects
cannot be trusted.

47
00:08:58.705 --> 00:09:00.498
We know where the traitor
has entrenched himself.

48
00:09:00.582 --> 00:09:03.168
If I fly directly
to the Footly stronghold--

49
00:09:03.251 --> 00:09:05.003
On a dragon. I presume.

50
00:09:05.086 --> 00:09:08.965
A beast well known for its delicacy
and precision in battle.

51
00:09:09.049 --> 00:09:10.842
Ah. yes. what a marvel.

52
00:09:10.925 --> 00:09:13.428
The flame it spews forth
can discern with pure magic

53
00:09:13.511 --> 00:09:15.096
who is blameless and who is deserving--

54
00:09:17.307 --> 00:09:19.392
I'll hear no more from those
whose greatest battle

55
00:09:19.476 --> 00:09:20.727
has been with their own indigestion.

56
00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:24.856
I am of the same mind as the lord
and ladies. Your Grace.

57
00:09:24.939 --> 00:09:27.025
Your army marches ever nearer.

58
00:09:28.485 --> 00:09:30.862
You will answer this outrage with force

59
00:09:30.945 --> 00:09:33.031
but discriminately...

60
00:09:35.825 --> 00:09:37.786
-...if we wait but a while longer.
-At what cost?

61
00:09:38.953 --> 00:09:41.081
Remember the prophecy.
your sacred calling.

62
00:09:41.164 --> 00:09:43.540
Whatever you do in its service
is justified.

63
00:09:43.625 --> 00:09:46.628
Aegon the Conqueror burned thousands
on the Field of Fire. thousands.

64
00:09:46.711 --> 00:09:47.962
and settled the realm for generations--

65
00:09:48.046 --> 00:09:49.339
The Conqueror

66
00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:51.341
burned enemy soldiers.
not subjects who bent the knee.

67
00:09:51.424 --> 00:09:53.468
Their lord bent the knee to you!

68
00:09:54.511 --> 00:09:56.346
The people would just as happily
follow a mule

69
00:09:56.429 --> 00:09:58.264
-if that same--
-My father would abhor it.

70
00:09:58.348 --> 00:10:00.183
Ah. and there we have it.

71
00:10:01.893 --> 00:10:02.894
But...

72
00:10:04.104 --> 00:10:06.564
my patience has its bounds.

73
00:10:06.648 --> 00:10:08.566
-I will send knives.
-So be it.

74
00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:11.111
At least I will get to meet
the fiend face-to-face before he dies.

75
00:10:11.194 --> 00:10:12.278
Oh. no. not you.

76
00:10:14.489 --> 00:10:16.074
I will have my satisfaction.

77
00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:18.743
Yes.

78
00:10:19.661 --> 00:10:21.913
But the most effective assassin
has a plain face.

79
00:10:23.623 --> 00:10:25.834
Fanatics still prowl the streets

80
00:10:25.917 --> 00:10:28.711
outside our castle gates
at Lord Ormund's bidding.

81
00:10:28.795 --> 00:10:30.505
That is your charge.

82
00:10:34.092 --> 00:10:37.220
Your Grace. there is a detachment
left here of Velaryon men. soldiers.

83
00:10:37.303 --> 00:10:39.055
ready to aid Prince Daemon in his--

84
00:10:39.139 --> 00:10:40.473
I think not.

85
00:10:45.061 --> 00:10:48.690
How many Velaryon men
remain in King's Landing?

86
00:10:48.773 --> 00:10:50.358
Some threescore. Your Grace.

87
00:10:50.441 --> 00:10:52.360
Petition your father for more.

88
00:10:52.443 --> 00:10:54.696
They may be needed to secure the city.

89
00:10:54.779 --> 00:10:56.948
Who then will you send to Tumbleton?

90
00:10:57.949 --> 00:11:01.536
It is a dangerous errand.
and one that will require force.

91
00:11:03.454 --> 00:11:06.875
My queen. the delegation
from House Baratheon has arrived.

92
00:11:08.918 --> 00:11:13.131
Your Grace. I am sent
to represent House Baratheon

93
00:11:13.214 --> 00:11:14.549
in response to your summons.

94
00:11:16.843 --> 00:11:18.052
Where is Lord Borros?

95
00:11:18.136 --> 00:11:20.346
Lord Borros begs patience. my queen.

96
00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:23.808
He has taken his army to the Red Mountains
to fight the Vulture King.

97
00:11:23.892 --> 00:11:26.686
who has been raiding the Stormlands
these many moons.

98
00:11:26.769 --> 00:11:28.771
His queen summons him north.

99
00:11:28.855 --> 00:11:31.774
and all of a sudden it occurs to him
that he must ride south.

100
00:11:33.026 --> 00:11:35.069
It is my lord's duty

101
00:11:35.153 --> 00:11:37.405
to guard the realm
against the Dornish threat.

102
00:11:37.488 --> 00:11:39.240
As it was his duty to guard my son

103
00:11:39.324 --> 00:11:41.784
when he came to treat
with him beneath his roof?

104
00:11:43.036 --> 00:11:44.996
Once the Vulture King has been subdued--

105
00:11:45.079 --> 00:11:47.874
Your lord makes the mistake
of considering a common bandit

106
00:11:47.957 --> 00:11:50.668
a greater threat
to his interests than I am.

107
00:11:53.421 --> 00:11:57.008
I could brand him a traitor
and hang you in his stead.

108
00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:03.973
No disrespect was intended. Your Grace.
to you or your endeavors.

109
00:12:04.057 --> 00:12:05.308
It is but...

110
00:12:05.391 --> 00:12:06.726
but a matter of time.

111
00:12:06.809 --> 00:12:08.102
Time?

112
00:12:08.728 --> 00:12:12.357
If there were aught else I could offer you
at this moment.

113
00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:14.567
I would lay it before you most willingly.

114
00:12:20.531 --> 00:12:21.824
Give me your belt.

115
00:12:54.357 --> 00:12:55.483
Anything to report?

116
00:13:01.781 --> 00:13:03.116
Market day tomorrow.

117
00:13:03.199 --> 00:13:04.867
Do you remember Market Day
in King's Landing?

118
00:13:06.703 --> 00:13:07.870
Before all of this?

119
00:13:11.332 --> 00:13:12.625
Fruit stalls.

120
00:13:14.294 --> 00:13:16.462
Geese honking. Traders shouting.

121
00:13:18.631 --> 00:13:19.674
Hot pies.

122
00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:24.470
Took it all for granted. didn't we?

123
00:13:25.388 --> 00:13:27.265
It will soon be the same again. I imagine.

124
00:13:27.974 --> 00:13:30.018
But we're not the same. are we?

125
00:13:30.101 --> 00:13:31.936
We weren't in service back then.

126
00:13:33.646 --> 00:13:36.899
At the beck and call of the queen
sleeping on a hill.

127
00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:38.735
alone.

128
00:13:40.862 --> 00:13:43.197
She stopped me going to the tavern. Hugh.

129
00:13:43.281 --> 00:13:44.991
Not one ale with the lads.

130
00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:48.828
What's the point in having a dragon
if no one's around to see it?

131
00:13:51.372 --> 00:13:53.583
Well. would you go back to where you were?

132
00:13:53.665 --> 00:13:55.668
Scrabbling around in the dust?

133
00:13:57.253 --> 00:13:58.379
No.

134
00:14:01.591 --> 00:14:03.885
Though I can't say my life
has been improved.

135
00:14:06.095 --> 00:14:07.263
Can you?

136
00:14:13.478 --> 00:14:14.312
Right. then.

137
00:14:22.278 --> 00:14:23.654
See you in two days.

138
00:14:25.406 --> 00:14:26.657
Ser Hugh.

139
00:14:30.411 --> 00:14:31.287
Come on. girl.

140
00:14:46.886 --> 00:14:48.054
Leave us.

141
00:14:53.768 --> 00:14:54.936
You would have done the same.

142
00:14:56.229 --> 00:14:58.606
Have I not shown you mercy

143
00:14:58.689 --> 00:15:02.527
even before those who named
my kindness to you a weakness?

144
00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:04.362
Are you so ungrateful

145
00:15:04.445 --> 00:15:06.614
-that you insist upon--
-Helaena is with child.

146
00:15:11.577 --> 00:15:13.871
So. you flee.

147
00:15:14.747 --> 00:15:17.500
To preserve the babe's life.
and Helaena's with it.

148
00:15:17.583 --> 00:15:19.961
Still you insist on misjudging me.

149
00:15:21.045 --> 00:15:23.131
If the child is male.

150
00:15:23.214 --> 00:15:25.049
would you not in the end
find it necessary?

151
00:15:27.552 --> 00:15:29.178
To hold him hostage. at the least?

152
00:15:30.763 --> 00:15:32.306
To draw out Aemond or...

153
00:15:33.182 --> 00:15:34.725
or Ormund in his pride?

154
00:15:36.602 --> 00:15:39.856
Or simply to secure your own reign
from endless challenges.

155
00:15:39.939 --> 00:15:41.983
You were discovered by guards.

156
00:15:44.986 --> 00:15:47.155
I cannot let this go unanswered.

157
00:15:47.238 --> 00:15:48.823
Helaena did as I persuaded her to do.

158
00:15:48.906 --> 00:15:51.075
If you must be cruel.
let it be me who suffers.

159
00:15:51.159 --> 00:15:52.326
Only spare her.

160
00:15:53.453 --> 00:15:55.455
You must both now
be more strictly confined.

161
00:15:56.247 --> 00:15:58.040
Your guard is doubled.

162
00:15:58.124 --> 00:16:00.376
There'll be no more walks in the Godswood.

163
00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:02.170
-I accept this judgment for myself--
-My judgment

164
00:16:02.253 --> 00:16:03.963
does not require your acceptance.

165
00:16:04.046 --> 00:16:05.756
Rhaenyra. you know what she is.

166
00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:08.050
She is fragile. you cannot confine her.

167
00:16:08.134 --> 00:16:09.677
I didn't!

168
00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.679
And now. I must!

169
00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:14.932
She cannot be seen.

170
00:16:15.016 --> 00:16:18.394
If she is known to carry Aegon's heir.
I will be forced to do what you fear.

171
00:16:18.478 --> 00:16:21.022
Well. so. so. so send us away
then to some remote--

172
00:16:21.105 --> 00:16:23.399
Away? Now?

173
00:16:24.734 --> 00:16:26.027
Your son is still at liberty.

174
00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:28.738
Your cousin wreaks chaos
within my city walls.

175
00:16:30.156 --> 00:16:32.950
Even today. I must answer another
of his murderous treasons.

176
00:16:35.244 --> 00:16:38.706
You are a Hightower.
To my court. you are the enemy.

177
00:16:39.665 --> 00:16:40.833
And to you?

178
00:16:43.336 --> 00:16:44.545
Do not try me.

179
00:16:50.927 --> 00:16:52.428
What did she tell you?

180
00:16:53.804 --> 00:16:55.556
Helaena is with child.

181
00:16:57.934 --> 00:16:59.644
Are there others who know?

182
00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:02.396
I believe not.

183
00:17:03.314 --> 00:17:04.857
You yourself had no suspicion?

184
00:17:05.775 --> 00:17:06.776
No.

185
00:17:08.027 --> 00:17:09.069
No.

186
00:17:20.122 --> 00:17:21.790
That one.

187
00:17:21.874 --> 00:17:23.834
A thief and a liar.

188
00:17:25.836 --> 00:17:27.463
Let me know when it's done.

189
00:17:44.939 --> 00:17:46.482
We will be avenged.

190
00:17:48.985 --> 00:17:50.820
If it takes a hundred years.

191
00:18:00.871 --> 00:18:02.164
What's this?

192
00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:07.962
Forgive me. my prince.

193
00:18:08.045 --> 00:18:09.714
This is how you answer?

194
00:18:11.632 --> 00:18:12.675
With desertion?

195
00:18:12.758 --> 00:18:14.927
The queen asked for loyalty.

196
00:18:15.011 --> 00:18:16.846
and I was willing enough to wait.

197
00:18:18.347 --> 00:18:20.558
But my children are now penniless.

198
00:18:22.101 --> 00:18:23.978
I will not leave them fatherless as well.

199
00:18:24.061 --> 00:18:26.814
Small wonder Hightower vermin
swarm our streets

200
00:18:26.897 --> 00:18:29.734
when they smell your craven stink.

201
00:18:29.817 --> 00:18:32.612
My first duty must be to my family.

202
00:18:33.696 --> 00:18:36.198
I will earn our coin another way.

203
00:18:36.282 --> 00:18:38.743
And when cutthroats
and scoundrels swarm your house.

204
00:18:38.826 --> 00:18:43.247
rip the bread from your children's mouths.
and take their pleasure with your wife.

205
00:18:45.666 --> 00:18:46.959
All of you.

206
00:18:49.086 --> 00:18:51.005
You forget what this city was!

207
00:18:52.715 --> 00:18:55.635
Before I turned this rabble into an army.

208
00:18:55.718 --> 00:18:58.929
before I led you out of your squalor
and formed you into men!

209
00:19:02.642 --> 00:19:03.643
Shame.

210
00:19:35.383 --> 00:19:37.677
Word in the city is that
you've done valiant work.

211
00:19:38.844 --> 00:19:40.429
The Triarchy raids have dwindled.

212
00:19:42.056 --> 00:19:43.265
There's more to do.

213
00:19:44.934 --> 00:19:46.560
As ever will be the case.

214
00:19:48.396 --> 00:19:49.814
State your purpose. Alyn.

215
00:19:49.897 --> 00:19:53.192
Ormund Hightower strikes
insidiously at King's Landing.

216
00:19:53.275 --> 00:19:54.694
seeking to throw it into chaos.

217
00:19:55.695 --> 00:19:57.697
The City Watch is buckling.

218
00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:59.323
I would send to Driftmark

219
00:19:59.407 --> 00:20:01.200
to shore up their number
with good Velaryon men.

220
00:20:01.283 --> 00:20:03.369
So. she asks more of me.

221
00:20:05.496 --> 00:20:07.581
It is I who ask.

222
00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.962
Do as you have said.
Her needs are endless.

223
00:20:14.672 --> 00:20:17.216
Have you not exhausted your anger yet?

224
00:20:17.299 --> 00:20:18.801
You take her side...

225
00:20:19.885 --> 00:20:22.430
when she yet refuses
to grant you legitimacy.

226
00:20:22.513 --> 00:20:25.975
And how many years did it take you
to do the same?

227
00:20:32.106 --> 00:20:33.524
I have heard things...

228
00:20:35.401 --> 00:20:37.611
in questioning these pirates.

229
00:20:39.363 --> 00:20:41.907
Tell her Tyland Lannister
survived the Gullet...

230
00:20:43.826 --> 00:20:45.494
and is making for Rook's Rest.

231
00:21:03.846 --> 00:21:06.265
-That's enough.
-The dogs will find him.

232
00:21:07.558 --> 00:21:08.851
They're welcome to him.

233
00:21:08.934 --> 00:21:10.436
By the time they come. we'll be gone.

234
00:21:10.519 --> 00:21:12.521
But not far. And if the others realize--

235
00:21:12.605 --> 00:21:16.650
If you wish to dig deeper. Lord Larys.
the shovel is free.

236
00:21:27.703 --> 00:21:31.165
I have found passage to Braavos
on a merchant cog out of Maidenpool.

237
00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:35.336
We must draw as little notice
as we can for a few days

238
00:21:35.419 --> 00:21:37.171
as we provision ourselves. but...

239
00:21:39.131 --> 00:21:41.258
I believe we can sail
before the full moon.

240
00:21:42.259 --> 00:21:43.928
I must interject. my king.

241
00:21:45.095 --> 00:21:48.808
I still feel it would be an error
for you to leave Westeros.

242
00:21:50.392 --> 00:21:53.062
You would be best served at Casterly Rock.

243
00:21:53.145 --> 00:21:56.065
where we can establish a court
and enjoin those still loyal to you.

244
00:21:56.148 --> 00:22:00.194
Do you think I'm a terrible man.
Ser Tyland?

245
00:22:03.697 --> 00:22:04.990
I would never say...

246
00:22:06.283 --> 00:22:07.368
That is...

247
00:22:08.536 --> 00:22:11.163
while I may not have always agreed
with every course of...

248
00:22:13.374 --> 00:22:14.208
Well...

249
00:22:17.461 --> 00:22:18.462
There is...

250
00:22:19.797 --> 00:22:22.216
in any one of us. I venture...

251
00:22:23.342 --> 00:22:26.554
much to admire and much to be deplored.

252
00:22:36.647 --> 00:22:37.648
Mm.

253
00:22:40.192 --> 00:22:41.819
We sail for Essos. then.

254
00:23:27.489 --> 00:23:28.741
For your face.

255
00:23:35.456 --> 00:23:38.042
It's been long since anyone
sought to defend me.

256
00:23:40.127 --> 00:23:41.921
I am in your debt.

257
00:23:43.464 --> 00:23:45.090
As I am apparently in yours.

258
00:23:46.216 --> 00:23:48.928
But I'm glad I can leave here now
with that score settled.

259
00:23:52.014 --> 00:23:54.016
Where do you think to go?

260
00:23:54.099 --> 00:23:55.601
I need to find my dragon.

261
00:23:56.602 --> 00:24:00.481
She would not have left me willingly.
and I'll not be without her.

262
00:24:04.026 --> 00:24:06.278
A frog in winter sleeps under the ice.

263
00:24:07.237 --> 00:24:08.781
Still and silent.

264
00:24:10.658 --> 00:24:11.825
Mend your wounds.

265
00:24:13.077 --> 00:24:14.411
Gather your strength.

266
00:24:15.788 --> 00:24:20.042
Let the world think you dead
until the spring thaw.

267
00:24:21.835 --> 00:24:23.170
I need to find a horse.

268
00:24:24.171 --> 00:24:25.756
To ride where?

269
00:24:26.715 --> 00:24:28.550
Over the numberless leagues
of the Seven Kingdoms?

270
00:24:28.634 --> 00:24:30.427
Vhagar will come to me.

271
00:24:30.511 --> 00:24:33.055
It is perhaps this forsaken castle
she shuns.

272
00:24:33.138 --> 00:24:35.391
Or if not. I'll go to King's Landing.

273
00:24:36.433 --> 00:24:38.227
It's said she haunted
the hills outside the city

274
00:24:38.310 --> 00:24:39.979
in the years before I was born.

275
00:24:40.062 --> 00:24:41.897
There is a bounty on your life.

276
00:24:44.149 --> 00:24:49.321
Every sellsword is combing the woods
hoping to slit your throat in the night.

277
00:24:51.115 --> 00:24:52.908
Oh. and half the commonfolk. too.

278
00:24:55.786 --> 00:24:57.579
Even you must sleep.

279
00:24:59.623 --> 00:25:01.959
There's no place for you
to rest your head.

280
00:25:03.210 --> 00:25:04.837
And nor am I safe here then.

281
00:25:06.547 --> 00:25:08.924
Or you. for harboring me.

282
00:25:10.718 --> 00:25:15.848
Is it possible that Vhagar flew away
as a way of protecting you?

283
00:25:18.642 --> 00:25:20.269
Without her. you're hidden.

284
00:25:22.479 --> 00:25:25.065
The queen assumes that
where your dragon is...

285
00:25:27.151 --> 00:25:28.777
there you will be. too.

286
00:25:33.782 --> 00:25:35.451
She is no queen.

287
00:25:35.534 --> 00:25:39.371
And when you find your mount.
will you fly to your death?

288
00:25:41.206 --> 00:25:43.500
Rhaenyra has six dragons to your one.

289
00:25:44.793 --> 00:25:47.087
You'll fall alone.

290
00:25:47.171 --> 00:25:48.464
And to what end?

291
00:25:55.179 --> 00:25:56.889
Never ceases to be fascinating.

292
00:26:06.648 --> 00:26:08.108
As you ordered. my lady.

293
00:26:21.747 --> 00:26:23.457
What did I say. when last we met?

294
00:26:25.417 --> 00:26:26.835
I saw Moondancer...

295
00:26:28.045 --> 00:26:31.632
my sister's dragon.
flying towards Iron Oaks.

296
00:26:31.715 --> 00:26:33.217
And what does that to do with you?

297
00:26:34.218 --> 00:26:36.136
She's my sister. I...

298
00:26:37.221 --> 00:26:39.223
I thought if I could just see her face.

299
00:26:39.306 --> 00:26:42.684
So you leave your hiding place.
in violation of our agreement.

300
00:26:42.768 --> 00:26:46.188
and you fly toward a town equipped
with several thousand pairs of eyes.

301
00:26:46.271 --> 00:26:49.399
all watching and wondering
what your appearance portends.

302
00:26:49.483 --> 00:26:51.527
I didn't even see her.
She was already gone.

303
00:26:51.610 --> 00:26:53.737
And what do you think
would have happened if she hadn't?

304
00:26:57.282 --> 00:26:59.785
The queen thinks
Sheepstealer's rider is dead.

305
00:26:59.868 --> 00:27:02.871
It has been your only reprieve.
If word reaches her...

306
00:27:05.749 --> 00:27:08.293
Have you forgotten already
the doom that hangs over you?

307
00:27:10.963 --> 00:27:12.214
And over me.

308
00:27:13.757 --> 00:27:15.092
For harboring you.

309
00:27:16.927 --> 00:27:19.012
For allowing myself to be swayed.

310
00:27:20.347 --> 00:27:22.099
-I'm sorry.
-Mm.

311
00:27:22.641 --> 00:27:26.270
All my life.
I have yearned after a dragon.

312
00:27:28.480 --> 00:27:31.275
And now I have one.
but I have lost everything else.

313
00:27:33.527 --> 00:27:34.820
That was your choice.

314
00:27:36.071 --> 00:27:37.531
They are dead to you now.

315
00:27:38.615 --> 00:27:41.535
But you got what you wanted. Go.

316
00:27:42.786 --> 00:27:44.872
And the next time
you try me will be the last.

317
00:27:55.090 --> 00:27:56.842
A bed would be more comfortable.

318
00:27:59.511 --> 00:28:00.596
My lady.

319
00:28:02.723 --> 00:28:03.765
I'm going.

320
00:28:04.766 --> 00:28:06.852
I just needed a little more time.

321
00:28:06.935 --> 00:28:10.022
I know what it is to be so weary.

322
00:28:13.400 --> 00:28:14.860
I...

323
00:28:15.527 --> 00:28:16.987
saw my father today.

324
00:28:19.531 --> 00:28:21.533
I was wondering if you would speak to him.

325
00:28:24.036 --> 00:28:28.165
There is a distance there.
as if he's removed himself entirely.

326
00:28:29.541 --> 00:28:30.751
I just thought...

327
00:28:32.211 --> 00:28:35.255
maybe now he might...

328
00:28:37.216 --> 00:28:38.383
see me.

329
00:28:41.178 --> 00:28:42.763
I thought the same with my father.

330
00:28:44.723 --> 00:28:48.977
They cannot face their ghosts.
so they seek to outstrip them.

331
00:28:50.562 --> 00:28:52.189
Even if they leave us behind.

332
00:28:54.107 --> 00:28:58.528
They roam. they punish.
they fight. they do.

333
00:29:02.741 --> 00:29:04.159
I cannot help him. Alyn.

334
00:29:05.702 --> 00:29:07.788
I have my own burdens to bear.

335
00:29:22.678 --> 00:29:23.762
I...

336
00:29:24.429 --> 00:29:25.889
You should go to bed.

337
00:29:39.403 --> 00:29:40.862
You're very dutiful.

338
00:29:45.867 --> 00:29:47.160
I am the eldest.

339
00:29:49.454 --> 00:29:51.081
It must get wearisome...

340
00:29:52.499 --> 00:29:54.668
attending to everyone else all the time.

341
00:29:58.422 --> 00:29:59.756
Maybe a little.

342
00:30:02.843 --> 00:30:04.678
Don't you ever want to forget it all?

343
00:30:06.430 --> 00:30:07.931
Do what you want?

344
00:30:32.622 --> 00:30:37.753
And so. Ser Criston fights on.
and yet you have returned.

345
00:30:37.836 --> 00:30:38.837
Because...

346
00:30:40.172 --> 00:30:42.007
Because fighting on is madness.

347
00:30:45.802 --> 00:30:48.180
Do you think me mad. Your Grace?

348
00:30:48.263 --> 00:30:50.307
No. sire.

349
00:30:50.390 --> 00:30:51.391
Hm.

350
00:30:52.351 --> 00:30:53.727
You mean to fight on?

351
00:30:54.728 --> 00:30:56.521
With what?

352
00:30:56.605 --> 00:30:58.774
There's a dragon
sitting on the hill above us.

353
00:30:58.857 --> 00:31:00.567
and five more not 30 leagues away.

354
00:31:01.276 --> 00:31:03.737
Rhaenyra will not burn her own subjects.

355
00:31:03.820 --> 00:31:05.197
She is a woman.

356
00:31:06.365 --> 00:31:07.824
Squeamish.

357
00:31:07.908 --> 00:31:11.411
If your host leaves these walls. it burns.

358
00:31:13.121 --> 00:31:16.166
Aemond has fled
and Rhaenyra holds my sister hostage.

359
00:31:17.167 --> 00:31:19.211
The River army draws closer by the day.

360
00:31:19.294 --> 00:31:21.380
What possible course is there?

361
00:31:21.463 --> 00:31:24.341
Your uncle lacks imagination
as well as courage.

362
00:31:27.344 --> 00:31:31.264
I would take one Hightower sword
over three of Tully's mudmen.

363
00:31:33.642 --> 00:31:37.312
When the usurper's host comes here.
we will fight on our terms. on our ground.

364
00:31:40.315 --> 00:31:42.150
We have the clear advantage.

365
00:31:43.318 --> 00:31:47.114
Meanwhile. we are turning King's Landing
against that overweening cunt.

366
00:31:47.197 --> 00:31:49.699
little by little. bite by bite.

367
00:31:50.951 --> 00:31:53.662
Exposing her as weak and unsuited to rule.

368
00:31:55.163 --> 00:31:57.374
The great houses cannot
but come to our side.

369
00:31:58.458 --> 00:31:59.835
Have any yet come?

370
00:32:01.920 --> 00:32:04.714
The patient hunter gets the kill.

371
00:32:07.342 --> 00:32:09.886
Something the craven among us
would do well to learn.

372
00:32:12.180 --> 00:32:15.892
I have marched a long road.
fought and killed.

373
00:32:15.976 --> 00:32:18.645
and suffered my comrades
to be killed about me.

374
00:32:18.728 --> 00:32:20.272
Yes. you have endured much.

375
00:32:22.107 --> 00:32:25.986
I'm sure you found solace
with some of your brothers in arms.

376
00:32:27.070 --> 00:32:29.114
I am fatigued.

377
00:32:29.197 --> 00:32:31.533
It's been weeks
since I've seen a feather bed.

378
00:32:32.534 --> 00:32:34.161
By your leave.

379
00:32:34.244 --> 00:32:37.164
You might see Ser Gwayne
to his quarters. Your Grace.

380
00:32:37.247 --> 00:32:38.748
Make sure he bathes.

381
00:32:43.920 --> 00:32:45.630
Oh. and...

382
00:32:46.965 --> 00:32:48.258
Mind yourself.

383
00:32:49.092 --> 00:32:51.011
Backs against the wall.

384
00:32:54.431 --> 00:32:57.225
-"Your Grace"?
-I'm sorry. I had to get through it.

385
00:32:57.309 --> 00:32:59.769
And this is your way? Fawning?

386
00:32:59.853 --> 00:33:01.188
Daeron.

387
00:33:01.271 --> 00:33:03.273
He's styled you the bloody king.

388
00:33:03.356 --> 00:33:04.858
You left me alone with him.

389
00:33:05.609 --> 00:33:07.068
You know what he is.

390
00:33:07.152 --> 00:33:08.820
I do what I can to keep him from...

391
00:33:10.030 --> 00:33:11.031
you know.

392
00:33:12.032 --> 00:33:13.658
I had no choice.

393
00:33:13.742 --> 00:33:15.160
No.

394
00:33:15.243 --> 00:33:17.454
But neither did it grieve you
to ride away.

395
00:33:21.082 --> 00:33:23.627
I hate what I am when I'm with him.

396
00:33:23.710 --> 00:33:26.671
A puppet. a fool. a child.

397
00:33:26.755 --> 00:33:29.299
And yet he means to put you
on the throne. apparently.

398
00:33:30.592 --> 00:33:33.011
Only as he cannot sit on it himself.

399
00:33:33.094 --> 00:33:35.680
No. he would thrust me forward
and devour me from within

400
00:33:35.764 --> 00:33:37.349
until there's nothing left.

401
00:33:37.432 --> 00:33:39.559
So tell him you won't do it.

402
00:33:39.643 --> 00:33:41.144
Then who will protect me then?

403
00:33:42.479 --> 00:33:45.273
Will you raise an army
against his savages?

404
00:33:48.652 --> 00:33:51.613
If you were king. you could cast him down.

405
00:33:51.696 --> 00:33:54.324
I will never be king. uncle.
we both know it.

406
00:33:56.868 --> 00:33:58.370
I need to lie down.

407
00:33:58.453 --> 00:34:00.497
-You'll stay. won't you?
-And do what?

408
00:34:01.790 --> 00:34:05.210
Bear witness whilst Ormund
marches our house to its doom?

409
00:34:07.003 --> 00:34:09.755
I'm second in line.
I shall return to Oldtown

410
00:34:09.839 --> 00:34:11.675
and prepare to pick up the pieces.

411
00:34:11.757 --> 00:34:14.928
Don't leave me again. Please.

412
00:34:15.011 --> 00:34:18.681
You're his little treasure now.
You'll be fine.

413
00:34:21.184 --> 00:34:23.103
When you were in King's Landing...

414
00:34:28.149 --> 00:34:29.693
Did you see my mother?

415
00:34:34.614 --> 00:34:36.324
Will you not eat?

416
00:34:40.411 --> 00:34:43.623
You have taken nothing since yesterday
and said little more.

417
00:34:50.589 --> 00:34:51.840
Helaena.

418
00:34:54.926 --> 00:34:59.139
Mysaria knew of our plan.
but she said nothing of Jaehaera.

419
00:35:01.266 --> 00:35:03.768
Was she truly stolen away to meet us

420
00:35:03.852 --> 00:35:06.855
at some secret place up ahead?

421
00:35:13.361 --> 00:35:14.529
I see.

422
00:35:17.157 --> 00:35:18.742
Forgive me. Helaena.

423
00:35:18.825 --> 00:35:22.162
The road ahead was fraught with peril.

424
00:35:22.245 --> 00:35:23.747
-To bring a small child--
-You lied.

425
00:35:26.583 --> 00:35:28.710
I wished only to save you from this place.

426
00:35:29.711 --> 00:35:30.879
Me?

427
00:35:32.464 --> 00:35:33.757
Or yourself?

428
00:35:36.426 --> 00:35:38.053
What difference does it make?

429
00:35:40.388 --> 00:35:43.850
I have come too far.
I have sacrificed too much.

430
00:35:45.560 --> 00:35:47.896
If I cannot at long last
salvage my daughter...

431
00:35:57.781 --> 00:35:59.240
Helaena. please.

432
00:36:01.743 --> 00:36:03.912
Please. you must eat.

433
00:36:37.737 --> 00:36:38.863
One-Eye.

434
00:36:48.415 --> 00:36:49.833
I have kept your secret.

435
00:36:51.042 --> 00:36:52.711
I will keep it still.

436
00:36:52.794 --> 00:36:54.421
You could have killed me. too.

437
00:36:55.547 --> 00:36:56.881
And claimed Rhaenyra's bounty.

438
00:36:58.091 --> 00:37:00.135
There are many things
I could have done to you.

439
00:37:02.011 --> 00:37:03.847
Then what is this game you play?

440
00:37:05.515 --> 00:37:06.975
It's yours to learn.

441
00:37:08.393 --> 00:37:10.019
If your spirit is willing.

442
00:37:29.581 --> 00:37:31.332
Have you forgotten your history?

443
00:37:33.001 --> 00:37:34.461
Dreamfyre.

444
00:37:34.544 --> 00:37:36.921
Your ancestor

445
00:37:37.005 --> 00:37:41.009
Rhaena Targaryen came to Harrenhal
after the death of her daughter.

446
00:37:42.218 --> 00:37:45.096
And she grieved and grew old here.

447
00:37:46.097 --> 00:37:48.892
Her dragon laid a clutch of eggs
before Rhaena herself died.

448
00:37:48.975 --> 00:37:53.605
and they have sat here.
cold and abandoned these hundred years.

449
00:37:55.356 --> 00:37:57.233
I do not know the ways of dragons.

450
00:37:57.317 --> 00:38:01.029
but I have long envisaged
the return of the Targaryens

451
00:38:01.112 --> 00:38:03.573
to this ancient seat.

452
00:38:10.789 --> 00:38:12.582
I have been cursed for my sins...

453
00:38:13.750 --> 00:38:14.834
Alys.

454
00:38:16.419 --> 00:38:19.047
All I put my hand to
withers beneath its touch.

455
00:38:20.340 --> 00:38:24.219
Do you imagine that you alone
know what it is to be cursed?

456
00:38:27.597 --> 00:38:30.642
I'm tired of this desolate existence.

457
00:38:32.477 --> 00:38:34.479
And so. I think. are you.

458
00:38:38.358 --> 00:38:41.069
You've been alone your whole life. Aemond.

459
00:38:43.321 --> 00:38:45.532
Can you not imagine...

460
00:38:46.825 --> 00:38:48.243
what it would be...

461
00:38:49.911 --> 00:38:52.163
to have it otherwise?

462
00:39:00.255 --> 00:39:01.673
It's warm.

463
00:39:07.178 --> 00:39:09.389
There's an ancient strength here.

464
00:39:11.140 --> 00:39:13.434
Let the gods turn their backs on us.

465
00:39:13.518 --> 00:39:15.770
We will make our own fortune.

466
00:39:18.731 --> 00:39:20.650
I will be the Lady of the Water.

467
00:39:23.444 --> 00:39:24.696
And you...

468
00:39:27.198 --> 00:39:30.869
the dragonlord by my side.

469
00:39:35.623 --> 00:39:38.376
But in the meantime.
you're a Targaryen prince.

470
00:39:40.670 --> 00:39:42.881
And your sons

471
00:39:42.964 --> 00:39:46.718
will be Targaryen princes in their turn.

472
00:39:56.686 --> 00:39:59.188
Tallow is scarce
and cost thrice what it did.

473
00:39:59.272 --> 00:40:00.899
We cannot light our sconces.

474
00:40:00.982 --> 00:40:02.442
You know my response.

475
00:40:02.525 --> 00:40:04.861
Ser Torrhen Manderly is Master of Coin.

476
00:40:04.944 --> 00:40:08.072
It is his task now to distribute
what resources we have.

477
00:40:09.032 --> 00:40:11.326
I suggest you address Ser Torrhen himself.

478
00:40:12.493 --> 00:40:13.912
Bring the next.

479
00:40:15.538 --> 00:40:17.582
Your Grace.

480
00:40:17.665 --> 00:40:20.919
The motherhouse
lately enjoyed the protection

481
00:40:21.002 --> 00:40:22.712
of the City Watch.

482
00:40:23.963 --> 00:40:26.049
Now. we are in peril.

483
00:40:26.966 --> 00:40:31.262
One of our girls
only last night was taken.

484
00:40:32.263 --> 00:40:34.265
You have my condolences. I shall...

485
00:40:36.351 --> 00:40:38.978
light a candle for her
when next I attend the sept.

486
00:40:42.732 --> 00:40:45.068
Godric. Your Grace. A mason.

487
00:40:45.151 --> 00:40:47.904
We have watched in fear
as we found gold cloaks murdered among us.

488
00:40:47.987 --> 00:40:51.407
and I have heard a great number of 'em
have resigned their posts.

489
00:40:51.491 --> 00:40:52.909
leaving the streets undefended.

490
00:40:52.992 --> 00:40:54.953
Yes. these are Hightower crimes.

491
00:40:55.912 --> 00:40:58.081
The craven Ormund strikes at me
from Tumbleton.

492
00:40:58.164 --> 00:41:00.917
where he has concealed himself
among innocents.

493
00:41:01.000 --> 00:41:02.085
This we know.

494
00:41:02.168 --> 00:41:03.878
But how will we now be protected?

495
00:41:03.962 --> 00:41:06.547
If the City Watch fails.
then who will preserve order among us?

496
00:41:06.631 --> 00:41:08.508
I have sent for Velaryon men

497
00:41:08.591 --> 00:41:10.551
to root out the enemy within our walls.

498
00:41:10.635 --> 00:41:12.178
Once they arrive.
the city shall be returned--

499
00:41:12.261 --> 00:41:13.888
How will they be protected?

500
00:41:13.972 --> 00:41:16.641
She was but six and 10!

501
00:41:18.810 --> 00:41:21.479
Your Grace. we are afraid.

502
00:41:21.562 --> 00:41:25.608
And wherever the fault lies.
we have none to look to now but you.

503
00:42:28.254 --> 00:42:29.589
Daemon Targaryen.

504
00:42:31.007 --> 00:42:32.800
How many?

505
00:42:32.884 --> 00:42:34.761
How many of you are there?

506
00:42:35.636 --> 00:42:38.181
-How many?!
-We have no number.

507
00:42:38.264 --> 00:42:40.058
We are everywhere.

508
00:42:43.728 --> 00:42:45.563
What did Ormund Hightower
promise you. gold?

509
00:42:45.646 --> 00:42:46.856
Huh?

510
00:42:46.939 --> 00:42:48.733
A place at his table
when he takes the throne?

511
00:42:48.816 --> 00:42:52.028
There is a king
waiting just outside these walls.

512
00:42:52.111 --> 00:42:54.197
And until Daeron the Daring
takes his rightful place.

513
00:42:54.280 --> 00:42:55.698
we will not rest.

514
00:42:55.782 --> 00:43:00.036
Then your kind will die in dragonfire.
or trampled down by my army.

515
00:43:00.912 --> 00:43:03.206
Will she lay waste to her own city?

516
00:43:03.289 --> 00:43:05.708
Will she set upon her own people
with swords?

517
00:43:05.792 --> 00:43:06.959
You'll never find us.

518
00:43:07.043 --> 00:43:08.503
We're the people of the Seven Kingdoms.

519
00:43:08.586 --> 00:43:10.254
We have no sign or sigil.

520
00:43:10.338 --> 00:43:11.756
And when you strike us.

521
00:43:11.839 --> 00:43:14.675
you only drive more to our cause.

522
00:43:16.636 --> 00:43:20.139
You rebel against one
who has neither wished nor done you harm.

523
00:43:21.182 --> 00:43:24.060
You can burn us. You can kill us.

524
00:43:24.143 --> 00:43:26.062
You will never make us embrace her.

525
00:43:47.083 --> 00:43:48.167
Watch where you're fucking...

526
00:43:49.794 --> 00:43:50.920
Your prince.

527
00:43:52.255 --> 00:43:53.089
Your Grace.

528
00:43:54.090 --> 00:43:55.633
What is your errand here?

529
00:43:55.716 --> 00:43:58.052
I-- I was-- I thought...

530
00:43:59.053 --> 00:44:00.429
I...

531
00:44:00.513 --> 00:44:01.639
I was just...

532
00:44:02.181 --> 00:44:03.599
I'm taking the air.

533
00:44:03.683 --> 00:44:06.227
Are you not commanded to stay
in the Keep under guard?

534
00:44:08.896 --> 00:44:10.022
Well. yes.

535
00:44:11.399 --> 00:44:13.526
In a manner of speaking.

536
00:44:13.609 --> 00:44:14.986
Insolent maggot.

537
00:44:15.820 --> 00:44:18.406
I'm up that bloody hill
for days at a time.

538
00:44:19.532 --> 00:44:21.492
Men deserve their simple pleasures.

539
00:44:22.827 --> 00:44:24.203
Keep us going.

540
00:44:25.413 --> 00:44:27.039
You yourself should understand--

541
00:44:32.128 --> 00:44:33.629
Set foot in the city again.

542
00:44:33.713 --> 00:44:35.590
and I'll put out your eyes.

543
00:45:22.637 --> 00:45:24.180
Ho. there.

544
00:45:25.014 --> 00:45:26.766
Ho. Friend.

545
00:45:34.690 --> 00:45:37.276
Come on! Put your backs into it!

546
00:45:39.820 --> 00:45:41.072
Come on!

547
00:45:44.700 --> 00:45:45.701
All clear!

548
00:45:47.411 --> 00:45:48.746
Here.

549
00:45:59.715 --> 00:46:03.511
The common man is. as a rule.
of no interest or concern.

550
00:46:03.594 --> 00:46:07.181
But you must never trust one
who's clawed his way to power.

551
00:46:07.265 --> 00:46:10.434
His ambition is oft fueled by some lack.

552
00:46:11.352 --> 00:46:14.730
Some shame. or lust. or rage.

553
00:46:16.565 --> 00:46:17.858
Mm.

554
00:46:17.942 --> 00:46:20.319
You should think on it
when you choose your Hand.

555
00:46:20.403 --> 00:46:23.406
Rhaenyra made a rare good choice
with Corlys Velaryon.

556
00:46:24.365 --> 00:46:26.492
There is a soundness to his breeding.

557
00:46:26.575 --> 00:46:29.161
Not the sordid appetite of the striver.

558
00:46:30.454 --> 00:46:31.831
What of my grandsire?

559
00:46:33.374 --> 00:46:34.959
Otto?

560
00:46:35.042 --> 00:46:36.585
Where do I begin?

561
00:46:36.669 --> 00:46:41.340
My lord. House Baratheon sends an envoy
to treat with the new king.

562
00:46:43.551 --> 00:46:46.012
Let the Stormlands lead the way.

563
00:46:46.095 --> 00:46:48.139
Highgarden will have no choice
but to follow.

564
00:46:49.640 --> 00:46:51.350
Ah. Stand up.

565
00:46:51.434 --> 00:46:52.643
Stand up. both of you!

566
00:46:55.104 --> 00:46:58.858
Lord Ormund Hightower.
Beacon of the South.

567
00:46:58.941 --> 00:47:03.946
Defender of the Citadel.
and Voice of Oldtown.

568
00:47:07.158 --> 00:47:08.743
Well met. Ser Ormund.

569
00:47:09.660 --> 00:47:12.288
I come as an envoy
of Lord Borros Baratheon.

570
00:47:12.371 --> 00:47:14.540
Lord Paramount of the Stormlands.

571
00:47:19.295 --> 00:47:22.590
-You are quite welcome. Ser...
-Ser Arrion Baratheon.

572
00:47:22.673 --> 00:47:24.633
Cousin to Lord Borros.

573
00:47:28.888 --> 00:47:31.849
I most regret presenting
ourselves to you in this state.

574
00:47:31.932 --> 00:47:33.809
The road was long and filthy.

575
00:47:33.893 --> 00:47:36.437
but I thought it best
to speak to you immediately.

576
00:47:36.520 --> 00:47:37.730
We are honored to receive you.

577
00:47:38.731 --> 00:47:40.733
And what word from Lord Borros?

578
00:47:40.816 --> 00:47:43.235
Well. House Baratheon
bends the knee to His Grace.

579
00:47:43.319 --> 00:47:45.780
King Daeron Targaryen.
and offers its many banners

580
00:47:45.863 --> 00:47:47.615
in alliance with House Hightower.

581
00:47:49.700 --> 00:47:51.702
I have been ordered to swear fealty

582
00:47:51.786 --> 00:47:53.996
to the new king on behalf of Lord Borros.

583
00:47:55.706 --> 00:47:58.209
Your lord has made a wise choice.

584
00:48:01.420 --> 00:48:05.466
If we might see the king in person.
that we may bend the knee before him.

585
00:48:08.844 --> 00:48:11.430
His Grace. Daeron Targaryen.

586
00:48:13.641 --> 00:48:15.101
The First of his Name.

587
00:48:17.144 --> 00:48:20.022
King of the Andals. the Rhoynar and the--

588
00:48:21.190 --> 00:48:22.441
No! Stop him!

589
00:48:22.525 --> 00:48:23.818
Stop him!

590
00:48:23.901 --> 00:48:25.236
-Stop him!
-No!

591
00:48:26.654 --> 00:48:30.282
These are assassins.
sent for Daeron and you.

592
00:48:45.589 --> 00:48:49.593
Ser Arrion Baratheon
has hair of light chestnut.

593
00:48:49.677 --> 00:48:52.471
He's about a foot taller.
and as it happens...

594
00:48:53.389 --> 00:48:54.348
far more comely.

595
00:48:59.145 --> 00:49:02.356
I will cleave the bitch
from crown to cunt.

596
00:49:03.357 --> 00:49:05.401
She will die wishing she never dared...

597
00:49:07.695 --> 00:49:08.737
Dared...

598
00:49:19.498 --> 00:49:20.499
Kat.

599
00:49:34.638 --> 00:49:36.682
I thought you were dead.

600
00:49:50.237 --> 00:49:52.072
I looked for you.

601
00:49:52.156 --> 00:49:53.949
I went home. but you'd gone.

602
00:49:54.033 --> 00:49:55.910
What choice did I have?

603
00:49:57.495 --> 00:49:58.704
I was alone.

604
00:50:00.164 --> 00:50:03.125
I escaped in the chaos.
I came here to my brother.

605
00:50:04.126 --> 00:50:05.711
And now. he's dead. too.

606
00:50:08.380 --> 00:50:10.049
But Kat. I've done it.

607
00:50:11.050 --> 00:50:12.676
I claimed a dragon.

608
00:50:13.594 --> 00:50:15.763
Vermithor. the Bronze Fury.

609
00:50:15.846 --> 00:50:17.515
I've been made a knight.

610
00:50:18.641 --> 00:50:20.476
And the queen has promised--

611
00:50:25.022 --> 00:50:26.607
Is that what this is?

612
00:50:28.025 --> 00:50:29.610
Dragon?

613
00:50:32.321 --> 00:50:35.074
-You smell different.
-We'll have coin now.

614
00:50:35.157 --> 00:50:36.992
A fine house. anything you wish.

615
00:50:37.910 --> 00:50:40.079
I can take you out of this to safety.

616
00:50:40.162 --> 00:50:41.413
Do you not see?

617
00:50:41.497 --> 00:50:44.124
Your husband is a dragonrider.

618
00:50:45.209 --> 00:50:46.919
Do you know how many days it takes...

619
00:50:48.212 --> 00:50:50.548
to walk the road here from King's Landing?

620
00:50:53.384 --> 00:50:57.429
Do you know what may befall
a woman alone on that road?

621
00:50:57.972 --> 00:50:59.640
Did something happen?

622
00:51:01.267 --> 00:51:02.893
Many things happened.

623
00:51:05.062 --> 00:51:08.482
While you were on Dragonstone...

624
00:51:09.441 --> 00:51:11.735
-seeking out your own glory.
-I did it for you.

625
00:51:11.819 --> 00:51:13.279
I didn't want it!

626
00:51:15.197 --> 00:51:18.409
I needed you here.

627
00:51:19.535 --> 00:51:21.120
On the ground.

628
00:51:25.791 --> 00:51:27.876
I'm sorry. I am.

629
00:51:27.960 --> 00:51:29.837
But I can stay no longer.

630
00:51:29.920 --> 00:51:31.630
If I am discovered here...

631
00:51:31.714 --> 00:51:33.299
Just come with me.

632
00:51:34.592 --> 00:51:36.510
I won't forsake my family.

633
00:51:38.804 --> 00:51:40.139
There is no time. Come. we're going.

634
00:51:40.222 --> 00:51:42.725
-No!
-I will not leave you in peril.

635
00:51:42.808 --> 00:51:44.059
What are you doing?

636
00:51:46.937 --> 00:51:48.147
Who are you?!

637
00:52:20.054 --> 00:52:21.680
You did well.

638
00:52:22.348 --> 00:52:25.059
I treated you harshly.
and for that. I'm sorry.

639
00:52:26.477 --> 00:52:28.312
The strains of the campaign.

640
00:52:32.024 --> 00:52:34.735
You may return to Oldtown if you wish.

641
00:52:34.818 --> 00:52:37.154
A small band of men won't attract
the attention of the dragons.

642
00:52:38.656 --> 00:52:40.491
-I'll not stop you.
-There are three of you.

643
00:52:40.574 --> 00:52:42.701
Should be easy. Again.

644
00:52:44.828 --> 00:52:46.372
He'd make a good king.

645
00:52:48.374 --> 00:52:49.958
Not that that matters to you.

646
00:52:54.213 --> 00:52:56.674
You think me so callous.

647
00:52:57.633 --> 00:53:01.011
I think you'd sacrifice lives
to feed your own pride.

648
00:53:03.639 --> 00:53:05.849
But I know you'd never sacrifice your own.

649
00:53:09.144 --> 00:53:10.396
So. tell me.

650
00:53:12.606 --> 00:53:13.982
What is your plan here?

651
00:53:18.070 --> 00:53:19.488
Speak your purpose.

652
00:53:21.156 --> 00:53:22.157
Helaena.

653
00:53:23.325 --> 00:53:24.785
She cannot stay confined.

654
00:53:26.203 --> 00:53:28.914
Her state of mind is precarious.
her condition being what it is.

655
00:53:28.997 --> 00:53:31.583
Do you have something useful for me.
or have I been misled?

656
00:53:34.962 --> 00:53:36.422
I know where Aemond is.

657
00:53:39.258 --> 00:53:41.844
-All this time?
-Only lately.

658
00:53:44.763 --> 00:53:47.224
I would need a guarantee
that we'd go free.

659
00:53:48.100 --> 00:53:49.476
Both of us. as originally agreed.

660
00:53:49.560 --> 00:53:52.312
You're in no place to demand
guarantees of anything.

661
00:53:52.396 --> 00:53:54.440
When Aemond is gone.
your reign is assured.

662
00:53:55.941 --> 00:53:57.109
Ormund will surrender or die.

663
00:53:57.192 --> 00:53:58.694
Helaena and I are no threat to you.

664
00:53:58.777 --> 00:54:00.988
We will disappear.
You will not hear of us again.

665
00:54:07.077 --> 00:54:08.620
Where is he?

666
00:54:09.747 --> 00:54:10.831
Harrenhal.

667
00:54:11.957 --> 00:54:14.460
My riders have searched for Vhagar there

668
00:54:14.543 --> 00:54:17.379
-half a dozen times.
-I did not say I know where Vhagar is.

669
00:54:20.966 --> 00:54:22.634
How did you come by this?

670
00:54:24.553 --> 00:54:26.013
There are times when Helaena...

671
00:54:26.972 --> 00:54:28.515
when Helaena sees things.

672
00:54:29.433 --> 00:54:31.143
It will sound mad.

673
00:54:31.226 --> 00:54:33.771
They are nightmares or puzzles.

674
00:54:35.939 --> 00:54:38.734
But the things she does see now and then.
they come to pass.

675
00:54:40.986 --> 00:54:42.446
She dreams.

676
00:54:44.573 --> 00:54:46.241
She's a dreamer.

677
00:54:48.035 --> 00:54:49.745
Like Daenys who foresaw the Doom.

678
00:54:56.126 --> 00:54:58.212
If what you say is true.

679
00:54:58.295 --> 00:55:01.590
if Aemond has separated
somehow from his dragon...

680
00:55:03.509 --> 00:55:04.635
then...

681
00:55:06.178 --> 00:55:08.305
he is one man on foot...

682
00:55:09.807 --> 00:55:11.141
and being hunted.

683
00:55:13.393 --> 00:55:15.479
He will have hidden himself
so he cannot be found.

684
00:55:15.562 --> 00:55:16.980
I have told you all that I know.

685
00:55:17.064 --> 00:55:19.483
His capture must now
fall to you and your council.

686
00:55:19.566 --> 00:55:20.567
No.

687
00:55:24.738 --> 00:55:27.199
If I send swords...

688
00:55:29.326 --> 00:55:31.245
he will flee again. go to ground.

689
00:55:31.328 --> 00:55:32.621
and be lost. but...

690
00:55:38.377 --> 00:55:40.003
If I send just one sword...

691
00:55:45.884 --> 00:55:47.678
with someone he trusts...

692
00:55:56.061 --> 00:55:57.771
No. I will be no part of this.

693
00:56:00.148 --> 00:56:03.443
-No. please. Rhaenyra.
-Unhand her Grace.

694
00:56:07.364 --> 00:56:08.365
I...

695
00:56:09.366 --> 00:56:10.617
I...

696
00:56:10.701 --> 00:56:12.411
I cannot leave Helaena.

697
00:56:18.750 --> 00:56:20.252
I will keep watch over her.

698
00:56:21.503 --> 00:56:22.921
Until you return.

699
00:56:28.886 --> 00:56:30.178
Did I not warn you...

700
00:56:31.597 --> 00:56:33.015
that you would come to this?

701
00:56:53.827 --> 00:56:55.370
I don't want to be alone.

702
00:56:58.165 --> 00:56:59.416
Nor do I.

703
00:57:01.251 --> 00:57:02.502
I have no choice.

704
00:57:07.132 --> 00:57:08.133
Here.

705
00:57:09.426 --> 00:57:11.136
You could refuse.

706
00:57:15.182 --> 00:57:16.892
And Aemond would still be like to die.

707
00:57:19.019 --> 00:57:21.063
Do you not wish to be free?

708
00:57:24.358 --> 00:57:25.734
Why am I here?

709
00:57:29.154 --> 00:57:31.698
Was there no other lord
that offered for my hand?

710
00:57:35.535 --> 00:57:41.458
Or was it your own desire
to marry me to my brother?

711
00:57:48.757 --> 00:57:50.384
It was my father's wish.

712
00:57:53.387 --> 00:57:54.930
But I did not begrudge it.

713
00:57:57.432 --> 00:58:01.395
Better here with me. I thought.
than a man you did not know

714
00:58:01.478 --> 00:58:03.855
in a place far away.

715
00:58:13.448 --> 00:58:15.909
Please. Please.

716
00:58:19.413 --> 00:58:23.583
We still have some
small chance at freedom. Helaena.

717
00:58:25.460 --> 00:58:27.796
But I cannot go unless I know
you are sustained.

718
00:58:31.258 --> 00:58:32.259
Please.

719
00:58:45.981 --> 00:58:47.232
There.

720
00:58:50.277 --> 00:58:53.613
I will return to you as soon as I am able.

721
00:58:53.697 --> 00:58:55.449
I give you my word.

722
00:58:55.532 --> 00:58:58.326
I will come back and collect you.
and we will...

723
00:58:59.244 --> 00:59:01.163
we will walk out in the sun.

724
00:59:29.983 --> 00:59:31.735
Forgive the hour. Your Grace.

725
00:59:34.571 --> 00:59:38.492
There has been a rider from Tumbleton.

726
00:59:47.084 --> 00:59:48.710
"Kick this dog...

727
00:59:49.836 --> 00:59:52.047
and it will bite your hand."

728
00:59:59.554 --> 01:00:02.390
You have fought like sharks.

729
01:00:03.725 --> 01:00:06.019
Swift and relentless.

730
01:00:07.604 --> 01:00:12.901
We have cut through our enemy
and routed them!

731
01:00:14.569 --> 01:00:18.156
But now. your blades
are needed in the city.

732
01:00:21.743 --> 01:00:23.036
And I...

733
01:00:24.663 --> 01:00:26.456
I have been too long away.

734
01:00:39.886 --> 01:00:41.054
Who are you?

735
01:00:42.472 --> 01:00:44.015
What's your errand?

735
01:00:45.305 --> 01:01:45.638
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
